","Organ":"kidney","Parameter":"H&E","Outcome":"no_change"}],"biodist":[],"biomarkers":[],"ic50":[],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Ir3","value":1.05,"value_relation":"=","std":0.02,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1016/j.dyepig.2023.111641","year":2023,"counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-003891","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"Distilled water and n-octanol were mixed vigorously for 24 h at 25 °C, to promote solvent saturation in both phases, before the experiments. A small amount of Ir1-Ir3 was added in a mixed solution of 3 mL of water (saturated with n-octanol) and 3 mL of n-octanol (saturated with water). The solution was shaken for 24 h and centrifuged at 5000 rpm for 10 min. The concentrations of the Ir1-Ir3 in both phases were measured by UV-vis absorption spectra. The oil/water partition coefficients were calculated using the equation: log Po/w = log (AO/AW), where AO and AW represent the absorbance of the complex in the n-octanol phase and water phase, respectively."}]}